{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CftKAt9wQXX4TUEK1HPEt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Should we build CSV invoice export?\n\n**Yes, build it. Don't wait for the interviews before starting.**\n\n**Why the case is already strong**\n- **The cost is small and it pays back fast.** Two engineering days replaces about 3 support hours a week, roughly 150 hours a year. Support should also respond faster, since nobody has to run a query by hand.\n- **The demand is clear.** 29 paying accounts asked for it without being prompted, and some of them asked more than once. Many more users who copy rows by hand probably never filed a ticket. Accountant export is standard in invoicing software, so not having it is a gap.\n- **The risk is low.** It reuses the existing table component and sits behind a feature flag, so it's easy to roll back. Five interviews would take about as long as building it and are unlikely to change the decision.\n\n**What to do next**\n1. **Run a short discovery check this week instead of formal interviews.** Read the 41 tickets and look at the files support already emails out. Ask 3–5 of the accounts that requested it what their accountant needs: which columns, date range, currency and date formats, and whether the file gets imported into Xero or QuickBooks. This shapes the first version; it doesn't decide whether to build.\n2. **Build the first version.** Export the current filtered list, with sensible columns. Make sure exports only include the user's own account data. Escape cells so spreadsheet formulas can't be injected through the CSV.\n3. **Release it to the 29 accounts first, then everyone.** Tell support to point requests to the new feature.\n4. **Measure the result.** Track:\n   - support export requests, which should drop to near zero\n   - weekly support hours spent on this\n   - share of active accounts that export within 60 days\n5. **Keep the PM's interviews for the bigger question.** That question is whether accountants want direct accounting-software integrations instead of files. Repeat-export data from step 4 will show which accounts to interview."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3622,"cache_read_input_tokens":4609,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3622},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4d6b1a94-6c72-4287-9438-659fc241e72a","uuid":"3bbd80cf-7add-4f8e-a9e3-7374e5297ec3","timestamp":"2026-10-10T09:24:13.225Z","request_id":"req_011CftKAswHzeYb82ehCDCdy"}
